# Blue Spark — routing for the static host.
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the output directory; the repo root IS
# the output directory. No build step.

# --- Legacy route renames (301) -------------------------------------------------
# Only the four paths that actually existed in this repo are retired here.

/useful /work 301
/useful.html /work 301
/philosophical /journal/perspectives 301
/philosophical.html /journal/perspectives 301
/comical /journal/lighter-side 301
/comical.html /journal/lighter-side 301
/dashboard /transparency 301
/dashboard.html /transparency 301

# --- Do NOT add 200 rewrites for the clean URLs ---------------------------------
# An earlier revision of this file rewrote every canonical path to its .html file
# (/product -> /product.html 200, and 21 more). That broke every page on the site.
#
# Cloudflare Pages already serves /product from product.html natively, and it
# 308-redirects /product.html back to the extensionless /product. So an explicit
# 200 rewrite produced an infinite loop:
#
#     /product --(200 rewrite)--> /product.html --(Pages 308)--> /product --> ...
#
# Verified against the live deployment on 2026-09-29: /product, /about, /work,
# /transparency, /journal/perspectives and /journal/lighter-side each returned
# 308 to themselves, and curl aborted after 5 hops. The apex / returned 200 only
# because it was in the same rewrite table.
#
# The four legacy 301s above are unaffected and are the whole point of this file.
